<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thutmose I</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thutmose I was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eighteenth-dynasty-of-egypt">Eighteenth Dynasty of Egypt</a> in the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a>. He led military campaigns deep into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubia">Nubia</a> and as far as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>, greatly extending Egyptian power. Accounts of the Egyptian Empire New Kingdom treat his reign as part of the empire's foundational expansion.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thutmose-i.jpg" alt="Thutmose I" width="280" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gary Todd from Xinzheng, China · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Egyptian_Sandstone_Head_of_Thutmose_I,_Karnak_(Thebes),_18th_Dynasty_(35727582483).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
